-- Make the geometry the only spatial extent of an alert config: the pipelines derive the admin areas from it.
-- Floods: the basin-based area of each GloFAS station, from {ISO3}_station_spatial_extents.geojson in the seed data (rodekruis/NRW-seed-data#26).
-- Drought and compound floods: the regions in src/seed/seed-data/seed-alert-config-spatial-extents.json, made from the former place codes.
-- Tropical cyclone and 'National' drought configs keep no geometry: they cover the whole country.
-- Rows that match nothing do not change. Flood configs without a geometry are kept; the pipeline skips them.
-- Then drop "spatialExtentPlaceCodes".

